The bundled Node.js Aphlict server has been removed. This directory and its
historical JSON file are retained only as a migration reference for the wire
protocol and must not be used to start a process.

Use the bundled `gorge-notification` service and configure its
`GORGE_NOTIFICATION_*` environment variables. Then point Phorge's
`notification.servers` setting at the compatible client and admin endpoints.
The `bin/aphlict notify` command remains available for sending a test
notification; the start, stop, restart, status, and debug commands are retired.

For more information, see "Notifications User Guide: Setup and Configuration"
in the documentation and the Gorge notification module guide.
